Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:07:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] v1.4.0 rebase: generated indexes (game-patches.md,
 env_switches.tsv)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the v1.4.0 rebase of the iOS ports (patches 0124-0131) leaves the generated patch index and switch table to bring up to date
Issue: HachebeDLC/NX2Apple#1

---
 docs/env_switches.tsv | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 38b4a32..04d70cc 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -289,8 +289,8 @@ DM_PREV_PROGRAM	switch	What `oe::GetPreviousProgramIndex` answers (default -1, s
 DM_PROBE	diagnostic	`=module:offset,…` (Mac only): puts a `brk` at each guest address and on every hit prints the thread, registers, strings they point to and a backtrace, then runs the original instruction
 DM_PROBE_ALL	diagnostic	Set: probe hits (`DM_PROBE`) also print x8–x18
 DM_PROBE_DUMP	diagnostic	`=module:offset:length[:file]`: on the first hit of any probe, writes that range of guest memory to a file (default `run/<platform>/probe_dump.bin`)
-DM_PROBE_EVERY	diagnostic	`=N`: every guest probe hit inside `DM_PROBE_FRAMES` counts, every N-th prints (its `#` is then the true hit count, for rates); `DM_PROBE_LIMIT` caps the printed ones
 DM_PROBE_DUMPTXT	diagnostic	with DM_PROBE, each pointer in the dump also shows the 96 bytes it points at as text
+DM_PROBE_EVERY	diagnostic	`=N`: every guest probe hit inside `DM_PROBE_FRAMES` counts, every N-th prints (its `#` is then the true hit count, for rates); `DM_PROBE_LIMIT` caps the printed ones
 DM_PROBE_FRAMES	diagnostic	Presented frame or inclusive `start-end` range in which guest probes print observations
 DM_PROBE_HEAP	diagnostic	`=<name>,<start>,<size>,<free list>,<used list>`: hex offsets of the sead heap layout the probes' `!xN` heap walk uses (default Mario's `0,28,30,b0,c8`)
 DM_PROBE_HEAPFRAME	diagnostic	`=<vtable offset in main>` (hex): the probes' heap walk treats heaps of that class as frame heaps (head +0xe0, tail +0xe8)
